\name{cellucid_field_summary}
\alias{cellucid_field_summary}
\title{Summarise a field per category}
\usage{
cellucid_field_summary(viewer, field, by, top = 50, visible_only = FALSE)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{A field by name: source "obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene; key is the name as shown. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}
\item{by}{The categorical obs field to group the cells by. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}
\item{top}{For a categorical field: at most this many of its categories per group. A whole number (at least 1). Default \code{50}, the viewer's own.}
\item{visible_only}{Only the cells the active view shows. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{by}, \code{field}, \code{groups}, \code{read_for} (For a gene read for a sample of the open cells: the cells its statistics are of). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
A continuous field or a gene per category of a categorical field (cells, mean, median, range, share above zero), or a categorical field's top categories per category.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{field.summary} (Dataset). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_field_summary(viewer, by = list(key = "cell_type",
      source = "obs"), field = list(key = "cell_type",
      source = "obs"))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
